# Announcements

# The agreements
rumc-treaty-trade-name = Trade agreement
rumc-treaty-trade-desc = The city and the faction trade on easy terms. The city gets money and a cut of the duty, and the ambassador of the faction gets points of influence.
rumc-treaty-preferences-name = Terms for a trade mission
rumc-treaty-preferences-desc = The faction opens a trade mission in the city on special terms. More money and a bigger cut, and the ambassador gets more points.
rumc-treaty-defense-name = Security agreement
rumc-treaty-defense-desc = The faction sends advisers on security. The calls of the third parties are cheaper, and the ambassador gets points of influence.
rumc-treaty-sanction-name = Close the market of the city
rumc-treaty-sanction-desc = The city shuts its market to the traders of the faction. The faction is offended, the others are pleased, the ambassador has a harder time with his mother faction, and the trade goes elsewhere.

# The petitions
rumc-petition-transit = The ambassador of the faction "{ $faction }" asks leave for its caravans to pass through the city. The faction will pay for the way.
rumc-petition-medical = The ambassador of the faction "{ $faction }" asks for medicine for the hurt. The help will be remembered.
rumc-petition-mining = The ambassador of the faction "{ $faction }" asks the right to mine on the outskirts of the city. They pay well, but it is mining on the lands of the city.
rumc-petition-patrol = The ambassador of the faction "{ $faction }" offers a joint patrol of the outskirts of the city and asks for money for it.
rumc-petition-technology = The ambassador of the faction "{ $faction }" offers an exchange of technology if the city pays a part of the cost.
rumc-petition-ultimatum-duty = The faction "{ $faction }" DEMANDS a lower duty of the city on its goods. Else the relations will be spoiled.
rumc-petition-ultimatum-payment = The faction "{ $faction }" DEMANDS a payment "for the trouble". A refusal will be taken as enmity.
rumc-petition-ultimatum-apology = The faction "{ $faction }" DEMANDS a public apology for the recent words of city hall.
